---
orbit 2026
page article
---
{# A rich-text page. Three things worth reading closely:

   1. `<title>` is RCDATA. Interpolation is allowed there and is escaped with
      the RCDATA rules, but an Html value can never render inside it (O2075).
   2. `<json-ld>` takes exactly one record expression and is serialized by the
      engine — strings are emitted with `<`, `>`, `&` and `/` escaped as \uXXXX,
      so the payload can never close the script element it lives in.
   3. The two Html obligations, side by side. `richtext` is declared
      `sanitizer`: merchant markup goes in untrusted and comes out safe, so it
      is SILENT at every use site — the sanctioned path should not generate
      warnings, or the warnings stop being read. `platformHtml` is declared
      `trustedHtml`: the platform authored that markup and asserts it is
      trusted, so it is emitted raw and warns every time (O2071 at check,
      O4902 at render). That second list is the audit surface. #}
<title>{article.title} - {shopName}</title>
<main class="article" id="main">
  <json-ld>{{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Article", headline: article.title, datePublished: article.publishedAt, url: article.url, author: {"@type": "Person", name: article.author.name}}}</json-ld>
  <header class="article__header">
    <h1 class="article__title">{article.title}</h1>
    <p class="article__byline">
      <if {article.author.avatar != none}>
        <img
          class="article__avatar"
          src={imgUrl(article.author.avatar, 96)}
          alt={article.author.name}
          width="96"
          height="96"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </if>
      <if {article.author.url != none}>
        <a class="article__author" href={article.author.url} rel="author">{article.author.name}</a>
      </if>
      <else><span class="article__author">{article.author.name}</span></else>
      <time class="article__date" datetime={article.publishedAt}>
        {article.publishedAt |> formatDate("MMMM D, YYYY")}
      </time>
    </p>
    <if {size(article.tags) > 0}>
      <ul class="article__tags">
        <for tag of={article.tags} limit={8}>
          <li class="article__tag">
            <a href="/blog/tagged/{tag |> slugify}">{tag}</a>
          </li>
        </for>
      </ul>
    </if>
  </header>
  <div class="article__body">{article.bodyHtml |> richtext}</div>
  <footer class="article__footer">
    <p class="article__summary">{article.excerpt ?? "Thanks for reading."}</p>
    {# Platform-authored, not merchant-authored: emitted raw, and the only line
       in this file that warns. #}
    <p class="article__legal">{legalNoticeHtml |> platformHtml}</p>
  </footer>
</main>
